    "group_total_term": {
      "description": "One term of a GROUP-BY total over the record axis: `value`[q] when record q carries the same `key` as record r, and 0 otherwise. Summed over q with the output index r it gives each record the total of its whole group, replicated onto every member - `total[r] = sum over q of [key[q] == key[r]] * value[q]`. isrm_line.esm uses it to recover each ROAD's length from the segment rows the road was cut into, which is the denominator that turns a segment's length into its share of its parent. It is a self-join: both index symbols range over the SAME record set, which is the same shape as the format's canonical prefix-scan spelling (esm-spec 4.3.1), differing only in the predicate. That makes it quadratic in the record count, and deliberately so - the alternative is a second index set sized by a metaparameter the layer would have to keep in step, and a group total that is wrong when a reduced run truncates the records. This one stays correct under truncation: the groups are simply smaller, and the shares still sum to 1 over whatever survives. `key` must be exactly comparable. An integer identifier read from a shapefile .dbf numeric column arrives as a whole-numbered float64 and compares exactly; a key that has been through any arithmetic does not, and would silently split one group into several. THE CONTRACTED SYMBOL IS `q` AND MUST NOT BE `t`. An index symbol is local to its aggregate (esm-spec 4.3.1) and `t` is as legal a name as any, but the Python binding's build-time hoist decides an observed is time-varying by asking whether the bare name `t` occurs anywhere in its body, without excluding names an enclosing aggregate binds. An aggregate that contracts over a symbol called `t` is therefore classified as state-dependent, silently drops out of the static materialisation, and becomes unreadable by observed_field - no error, no warning, just a missing observed and every observed downstream of it missing too. See BUGS.md.",
      "params": [
        "key",
        "value"
      ],
      "body": {
        "op": "*",
        "args": [
          {
            "op": "ifelse",
            "args": [
              {
                "op": "==",
                "args": [
                  {
                    "op": "index",
                    "args": [
                      "key",
                      "q"
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "op": "index",
                    "args": [
                      "key",
                      "r"
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              },
              1.0,
              0.0
            ]
          },
          {
            "op": "index",
            "args": [
              "value",
              "q"
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    }
  }
